# =========================================================
# NESTJS CLI USAGE POLICY
# =========================================================
## CLI First Strategy

Always try to use a CLI command before manually modifying files.

### ✅ Example CLI Workflow
- Creating modules, controllers, services:
  - `nest g module users`
  - `nest g controller users`
  - `nest g service users`
- Creating DTOs / Guards / Pipes / Interceptors:
  - `nest g class users/dto/create-user.dto --flat`
  - `nest g guard auth`
  - `nest g interceptor logging`

### ❌ Only write files manually when:
- Nest CLI does not support structure needed
- Scaffolding requires custom patterns (e.g., DDD aggregates)
- You explain why manual creation was chosen

